d 'DATADICTIONARY': module to enhanced, over-time-ready codebook generator for multi-wave data
d
d  A modern descsave. datadictionary builds an Excel codebook that
d puts each variable's statistics, % missing, distinct count,
d common values, labels, and notes side by side (one row per
d variable, or per variable-wave over time), including the srctag
d char written by combineall/projectbuilder. Results go to the
d screen, a machine-readable .dta, and a multi-sheet workbook, with
d clickable links to open them. For a study run in waves, files() /
d folder() stack a per-wave row per variable and add a "changed"
d column flagging any variable whose label or category set shifted
d since the previous wave (only detectable from the original wave
d files, since stitching destroys per-wave value labels). In-memory
d mode can also write a capture-guarded relabel do-file (dofile())
d that re-applies labels, formats, notes, and chars after a
d CSV/Excel round-trip through another package, with a re-ingestion
d receipt, plus an optional infile dictionary (dictionary()). 
d
d KW: codebook; data documentation; data management; Excel
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.0
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f datadictionary.ado
f datadictionary.sthlp
